    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey so my monstera deliciosa is starting to look kinda weird. some of the lower leaves are turning yellow and they feel a bit soft. i think im watering it once a week but i cant tell if im doing too much or if it just needs more food? any idea what might be happening?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yellowing and soft lower leaves on a Monstera deliciosa are often a sign of overwatering, which is a common issue with these tropical plants. It's very easy to accidentally soak them too much, which can lead to root rot. You might want to check the soil moisture deeper down, not just the surface, and let the top few inches dry out between waterings. If it's consistently wet, try letting it dry out more thoroughly before giving it another drink.",
